{"name":"Lionheart","hex":"#cc2222","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Lionheart","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An epithet of Richard I of England."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Lionheart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Richard I of England","blocks":[{"text":"Richard I, known as Richard the Lionheart or Richard Cœur de Lion because of his reputation as a great military leader and warrior, was King of England from 1189 until his death in 1199. He also ruled as Duke of Normandy, Aquitaine, and Gascony; Lord of Cyprus; Count of Poitiers, Anjou, Maine, and Nantes; and was overlord of Brittany at various times during the same period. He was the third of five sons of Henry II of England and Eleanor of Aquitaine and was therefore not expected to become king, but his two elder brothers predeceased their father."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg/330px-Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_I_of_England","wikidata":"Q42305"},{"title":"Lionheart (1990 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lionheart is a 1990 American martial arts film directed by Sheldon Lettich, starring Jean-Claude Van Damme, Deborah Rennard, Harrison Page, Lisa Pelikan and Brian Thompson. It also features the acting debut of Ashley Johnson. Van Damme plays a French Foreign Legionnaire stationed in Africa, who must desert to the United States and enter the underground fighting circuit to raise money for his murdered brother's family."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/72/Lion-Heart-Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lionheart_(1990_film)","wikidata":"Q581960"},{"title":"Lionheart (Kate Bush album)","blocks":[{"text":"Lionheart is the second studio album by the English singer-songwriter Kate Bush. It was released on 10 November 1978, nine months after Bush's successful debut album The Kick Inside. Lionheart peaked at No. 6 on the UK Albums Chart, and has been certified Platinum by the BPI."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/Katebushlionheart.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lionheart_(Kate_Bush_album)","wikidata":"Q1754603"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg/500px-Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg/1280px-Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg/500px-Church_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChurch_of_Fontevraud_Abbey_Richard_I_effigy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Seal_-_Richard_I_of_England.jpg/500px-Seal_-_Richard_I_of_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Seal_-_Richard_I_of_England.jpg/1280px-Seal_-_Richard_I_of_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Seal_-_Richard_I_of_England.jpg/500px-Seal_-_Richard_I_of_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"King Richard I's Great Seal of 1189","link":"https://